accepted answers:
Solved! It was a little mistake in the configure method in the config class, where I didn't change

...
@Override
    protected void configure(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        super.configure(http);
        http.logout().logoutSuccessUrl("/home")
                .and()
                .authorizeRequests()
                .antMatchers("/**").hasAuthority("user");
    }
...
and It has to be

...
@Override
    protected void configure(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        super.configure(http);
        http.logout().logoutSuccessUrl("/home")
                .and()
                .authorizeRequests()
                .antMatchers("/**").hasAuthority("ROLE_USER");
    }
...
Now the error 403 doesn't appear, but now the /home page doesn't show.

